+// ATHAN PATCH 1 (esp32_athan, on ESPHome 2026.9.1): a speaker applies a stream's format (sample rate, channels) when
+// it starts, and keeps converting from the format it started with while it runs. Upstream gives it the format once,
+// at the first parsed frame header, so audio plays at the wrong speed and pitch when
+//   - microMP3 locked onto a false header inside a frame (joining a live stream mid-frame): its first format is
+//     wrong, and at the first real frame it reports MP3_STREAM_INFO_CHANGED, which upstream ignores;
+//   - the stream really changes format (a radio station moving to a recording encoded differently);
+//   - a new stream starts while the speaker still runs from the one before.
+// So the format is handed over only to a stopped speaker, and handed over again whenever the decoder's format
+// changes. The decoder's next write restarts the speaker (play() starts a stopped speaker) with the new format.
+// See firmware/components/speaker/README.md.
+static void athan_stop_speaker_for_format(speaker::Speaker *spk) {
+  if (spk->is_stopped())
+    return;
+  spk->stop();
+  for (int i = 0; i < 100 && !spk->is_stopped(); i++)  // at most 1 s
+    vTaskDelay(pdMS_TO_TICKS(10));
+}
